From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:29:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Limit safe abspos overflow by the original containing block
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

css-align-3 §4.4.1.2 gives absolutely positioned boxes the same rule
for `safe` as for the default overflow alignment: a box that overflows
its inset-modified containing block stays aligned as specified as far as
the overflow limit rect allows, and only start-aligns in that rect when
it does not fit. The limit rect is the bounding rect of the IMCB and the
original containing block, the one before grid placement narrowed it to
a grid area.

`safe` instead fell back to the start of the IMCB as soon as the box
overflowed it, and the default rule bounded the overflow by the grid
area instead of the grid's padding box. A box at its static position
(both insets auto) keeps ignoring the default rule: every engine aligns
it unsafely there, and the css-flexbox and css-grid abspos static
position tests expect that. WPT ed5a113c changed
css-grid/abspos/grid-abspos-staticpos-align-self-safe-001-ref.html to
this behaviour (Safari passes it; Chrome and Firefox do not).

Upstream Taffy (main) has the same start-of-IMCB fallback for `safe`.
